task:
  id: zcode-source-auth-router-rebuild
  date: 2026-08-24
  status: in_progress
  objective: >-
    Rebuild ZCode authentication, Z.AI endpoint selection, GLM model parameters,
    and Ciel Runtime router integration from verified source, official
    documentation, and live execution evidence only.

evidence:
  upstream_source:
    repository: https://github.com/kingsword09/zcode-cli.git
    package: zcode-app-cli@3.8.1-15
    tag: v3.8.1-15
    commit: e6e110cba0b41d72bc1f7ee1e146facbe227d81a
    bundled_runtime: 0.16.3
    facts:
      - src/zai-oauth.ts fixes the OAuth redirect URI to zcode://zai-auth/callback.
      - scripts/sync-runtime.ts exchanges the callback at https://zcode.z.ai/api/v1/oauth/token.
      - The returned OAuth access token is resolved to a Coding Plan API key and written to provider zai.
      - The public CLI source contains no Start Plan routed-provider implementation.
      - The public CLI documents browser OAuth as macOS-only and API-key/custom-provider access as cross-platform.
  official_zai_docs:
    tool_integration: https://docs.z.ai/devpack/tool/others
    glm_5_3: https://docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-5.3
    verified_coding_plan_base_urls:
      anthropic_messages: https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic
      openai_chat: https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4
      openai_responses: https://api.z.ai/api/v1
    verified_glm_5_3_contract:
      context_tokens: 1000000
      max_output_tokens: 128000
      thinking_type: enabled
      reasoning_effort: [low, high, max]
      default_reasoning_effort: max
  mia_control:
    host: mia@100.95.132.58
    installed_ciel: 0.2.36-nightly.20260825-022132.97b7e85
    installed_zcode_app_cli: 3.8.1-15
    installed_zcode_runtime: 0.16.3
    native_zcode_config:
      provider: zai
      kind: anthropic
      base_url: https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic
      has_api_key: true
    ciel_workspace_config:
      selected_provider: zai-start-plan
      coding_plan_has_api_key: false
      start_plan_has_api_key: false
    native_model_request:
      result: rejected
      http_status: 429
      provider_code: 1113
      provider_message: Insufficient balance or no resource package. Please recharge.
      interpretation: >-
        Authentication reached the Coding Plan provider and received a provider
        business response, but the account credential had no usable Coding Plan
        balance or resource package. This is not evidence that Start Plan quota
        is available through the open-source CLI route.

contradictions_found:
  - >-
    Ciel Runtime currently treats the OAuth JWT as a Start Plan model credential,
    but the public CLI source stores that JWT as login state and resolves a
    separate Coding Plan API key for model access.
  - >-
    Ciel Runtime currently tries undocumented oauth/cli/init and oauth/cli/poll
    routes before the source-backed authorization-code flow.
  - >-
    Ciel Runtime currently registers Coding Plan as OpenAI Chat plus Anthropic,
    while current official documentation also publishes an OpenAI Responses base URL.
  - >-
    Ciel Runtime's localhost OAuth redirect differs from the registered
    zcode://zai-auth/callback URI in the exact public source tag.

changes:
  authentication:
    - Removed Ciel-owned oauth/cli/init and oauth/cli/poll requests.
    - Removed the localhost OAuth callback receiver.
    - Delegated login to the installed public zcode-app-cli launcher.
    - Validated and imported only provider.zai kind=anthropic with the documented Anthropic Coding Plan base URL.
    - Shared the resolved Coding Plan API key through the zai-coding-plan profile for every runtime client.
    - Rejected Start Plan JWT import as a routed model credential.
  endpoints:
    anthropic_messages: https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic/v1/messages
    openai_chat: https://api.z.ai/api/coding/paas/v4/chat/completions
    openai_responses: https://api.z.ai/api/v1/responses
    implementation: provider operation base URL selection plus native Responses passthrough wiring
  start_plan:
    - Preserved existing stored profile values.
    - Blocked launch and header generation because no public model endpoint contract was verified.
    - Removed the speculative CAPTCHA, gateway header, and provider-3012 rewrite paths.
  model_parameters:
    glm_5_3:
      context_tokens: 1000000
      max_output_tokens: 131072
      thinking_type: enabled
      reasoning_effort: [low, high, max]
      default_reasoning_effort: max
      temperature_when_supplied: 1.0
    glm_5_2:
      context_tokens: 1000000
      max_output_tokens: 131072
    glm_5_1:
      context_tokens: 200000
      max_output_tokens: 131072

verification:
  source_checkout: passed
  official_document_review: passed
  mia_native_control: passed_with_provider_rejection
  code_changes: passed
  local_tests:
    command: python -m unittest discover -s tests
    result: passed
    tests_run: 2746
    skipped: 136
    elapsed_seconds: 297.542
  isolated_router_wire:
    command: python docs/journal/2026/08/24/evidence/verify-zai-coding-plan-router.py
    result: passed
    downstream_status: completed
    upstream_path: /v1/responses
    authorization: bearer_present
    x_api_key: present
    normalized_model: glm-5.3
    normalized_thinking: enabled
    normalized_reasoning_effort: max
    normalized_temperature: 1.0
  live_routed_model_response: blocked_by_mia_account_provider_code_1113
